  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Iron oxide <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>FeO</mi></math>, crystallises in a cubic lattice with a unit cell edge length of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8491;</mo></math>. If density of the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>FeO</mi></math> in the crystal is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>, then the number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>FeO</mi></math>&nbsp;units present per unit cell is _____ (Nearest integer)</p><p>Given : Molar mass of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Fe</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>56</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> respectively.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>23</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The density of the crystal can be calculated as follows,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>density</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>effective</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>number</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>of</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>atoms</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Molar</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mass</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>Avogadro</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>number</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Edge</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>length</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>72</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>23</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>125</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>166</mn><mo>&#8771;</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p>"
  }
